	(text "microSD: SDIO 1-bit, switched by a TPS22917"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 220.98 20.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "0dc87690-228e-4283-9151-f0aae15ca86c")
	)
	(text "TPS22917: SD_EN (PA7) high = card on, 100k pull-down keeps it off through reset.\nCT 1n (as on the BT switch) slows the rise to limit the inrush. QOD through R611:\ndischarges SD_VDD when off. JP603 bypasses the switch, JP602 is the drain jumper.\n\nBack-powering: CMD/DAT pull-ups (47k) sit on SD_VDD, never on +3.3V. Before pulling\nSD_EN low, put PC12 / PD2 / PC8 in analog mode. Never cut power during a write.\n\n1-bit mode: DAT1-DAT3 unused but pulled up (DAT3 high = SD mode at CMD0).\nR612-R614: 0R, R612 can become 22-33R if CLK rings.\nCard detect (DM3AT datasheet): switch A-B open without a card, closed with one.\nA on GND, B on SD_CD with R620 on the always-on +3.3V, so detect works while the\ncard is off. SD_CD (PA8, EXTI8): low = card in."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 220.98 190.5 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3df4fbb0-ee71-48d0-9abf-19e363bde9d0")
	)
	(text "CE# pull-up: the datasheet (section 7) wants CE# high and CLK / SIO0-3 low from the\npower ramp to tPU = 150 us after it, then a RESET command (0x66, 0x99). No pull-ups\non SIO2/SIO3: they would hold them high, and the chip ignores them in SPI mode.\n\nR601-R606: 0R footprints, become 22-33R (series termination) if the 90 MHz edges\nring. Place them next to the MCU, keep the six lines short and matched, GND under them.\n\nSPI fallback: same pins. QUADSPI runs single-line (plain SPI, mode 0):\nSI = IO0 (PE7), SO = IO1 (PE8), CLK = PB2, CE# = PC11. Commands 0x03 / 0x0B / 0x02.\nQuad: 0x35 enters QPI, 0xEB / 0x38 quad read / write. PE7-PE10 have no SPI\nalternate function, so the last resort is bit-banging the same pins.\ntCEM: CE# low for 8 us max, the firmware splits long transfers."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 109.22 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4c57d296-6ac3-4262-94aa-23d1bb18ffc8")
	)
	(text "PSRAM: APS6404L-3SQN (8 MB, 3.3 V) on QUADSPI bank 2"
